<date>2026-10-22</date>
<releaseinfo>0.2.4</releaseinfo>

<abstract>
<para>
&kappname; is a tool to inspect and debug servers implementing the
Model Context Protocol (<acronym>MCP</acronym>). It connects to a server
as an <acronym>MCP</acronym> client, lets you send requests to it and shows
the exchanged messages.
</para>
</abstract>

<keywordset>
<keyword>KDE</keyword>
<keyword>MCP</keyword>
<keyword>Model Context Protocol</keyword>
<keyword>inspector</keyword>
<keyword>debug</keyword>
<keyword>kmcpclientinspector</keyword>
</keywordset>

</bookinfo>

<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>

<para>
The Model Context Protocol (<acronym>MCP</acronym>) is an open protocol which
allows applications to expose tools, prompts and resources to clients such as
<acronym>AI</acronym> assistants. Messages are exchanged using JSON-RPC.
</para>

<para>
&kappname; acts as an <acronym>MCP</acronym> client. It allows developers
of <acronym>MCP</acronym> servers to:
</para>

<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>manage a list of <acronym>MCP</acronym> servers;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>connect to a server and see the result of the initialization handshake;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>list and call the tools provided by the server;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>list and retrieve the prompts provided by the server;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>list the resources and resource templates provided by the server;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>check that the server answers with a ping request;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>look at every JSON-RPC message sent and received;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>follow the log notifications emitted by the server.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

</chapter>

<chapter id="using-kapp">
<title>Using &kappname;</title>

<sect1 id="main-window">
<title>The Main Window</title>

<para>
The main window is divided in two parts:
</para>

<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>
On the left, the list of the configured <acronym>MCP</acronym> servers.
From there you can add, modify, remove, enable or disable a server.
</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>
On the right, one tab for each enabled server. Disabled servers do not get
a tab.
</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>
When a new version brings new features, a message is shown at the top
of the window the first time &kappname; is started. The complete list of
changes is available with <menuchoice><guimenu>Help</guimenu><guimenuitem>What's new</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="server-tab">
<title>The Server Tab</title>

<para>
Each server tab is split in two parts: the server settings on the left and
the actions on the right.
</para>

<sect2 id="server-settings">
<title>Server Settings</title>

<para>
The upper part shows information about the server:
</para>

<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Name:</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>The name of the server.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Type:</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>How &kappname; communicates with the server: by starting a
local process, or through a network <acronym>URL</acronym>.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Command:</guilabel>, <guilabel>Arguments:</guilabel>, <guilabel>Environment:</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>For a local server, the program started by &kappname;, its
arguments and the environment variables passed to it.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Url:</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>For a remote server, the address used to reach it.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Roots:</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>The roots (directories or files) exposed to the server.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>

<para>
The <guilabel>Capabilities</guilabel> group lets you choose which client
capabilities are announced to the server during initialization:
<guilabel>Elicitation</guilabel>, <guilabel>Roots</guilabel> and
<guilabel>Sampling</guilabel>. They are all enabled by default. They can only
be changed while the server is disconnected.
</para>

<para>
The <guibutton>Edit…</guibutton> button opens a dialog to modify the server
settings. It is disabled while the server is connected.
</para>

<para>
Use the <guibutton>Connect</guibutton> button to start the client and send the
initialization request to the server, and the <guibutton>Disconnect</guibutton>
button to stop it.
</para>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="actions">
<title>Actions</title>

<para>
The right part of the server tab contains one tab for each kind of request
or information:
</para>

<variablelist>

<varlistentry id="action-initialize">
<term><guilabel>Initialize</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
Shows the JSON answer of the server to the initialization request: protocol
version, server information and server capabilities.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-ping">
<term><guilabel>Ping</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The <guibutton>Ping</guibutton> button sends a ping request, to check that the
server is still answering.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-list-tools">
<term><guilabel>List Tools</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The <guibutton>List Tools</guibutton> button asks the server for the list of
the tools it provides and shows the answer.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-call-tool">
<term><guilabel>Call Tool</guilabel></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Click on <guibutton>List Tools</guibutton> to fill the list of tools; the
<guilabel>Search</guilabel> field filters it. Select a tool: its arguments
are shown, with a field adapted to each argument type (text, integer,
number, boolean, or JSON value). Check
<guilabel>Edit arguments as JSON</guilabel> to write all the arguments
directly as a JSON object.
</para>
<para>
Click on <guibutton>Call Tool</guibutton> to call the tool. Required arguments
and argument types are checked before the request is sent. The result is
shown in two tabs:
</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><guilabel>Content</guilabel>: a readable view of the
returned content (text, images, audio, resource links, embedded resources
and structured content), and whether the tool succeeded or returned
an error;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guilabel>JSON</guilabel>: the raw JSON answer.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-list-prompts">
<term><guilabel>List Prompts</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The <guibutton>List Prompts</guibutton> button asks the server for the list of
the prompts it provides and shows the answer.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-get-prompt">
<term><guilabel>Get Prompt</guilabel></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Click on <guibutton>List Prompts</guibutton> to fill the list of prompts; the
<guilabel>Search</guilabel> field filters it. Select a prompt, fill in its
arguments, then click on <guibutton>Get Prompt</guibutton>. The result is
shown in two tabs:
</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><guilabel>Messages</guilabel>: the messages of the prompt,
with their role (<guilabel>User</guilabel> or
<guilabel>Assistant</guilabel>);</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><guilabel>JSON</guilabel>: the raw JSON answer.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-list-resources">
<term><guilabel>List Resources</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The <guibutton>List Resources</guibutton> button asks the server for the list
of the resources it provides and shows the answer.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-resource-templates">
<term><guilabel>Resource Templates</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The <guibutton>Resource Templates</guibutton> button asks the server for the
list of its resource templates and shows the answer.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-log">
<term><guilabel>Log</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
Lists every JSON-RPC message exchanged with the server, with its
<guilabel>Identifier</guilabel>, <guilabel>Method Name</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Time</guilabel>, <guilabel>Duration</guilabel> and
<guilabel>Direction</guilabel> (<guilabel>Sent</guilabel> or
<guilabel>Received</guilabel>). Use the <guilabel>Search</guilabel> field to
filter the list. Selecting a message shows its JSON content.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry id="action-server-notification">
<term><guilabel>Server Notification</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
Shows the log messages sent by the server, with their
<guilabel>Time</guilabel>, <guilabel>Level</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Logger</guilabel> and <guilabel>Message</guilabel>. The
<guilabel>Minimum level:</guilabel> list hides the messages below the
selected level (<guilabel>Debug</guilabel>, <guilabel>Info</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Notice</guilabel>, <guilabel>Warning</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Error</guilabel>, <guilabel>Critical</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Alert</guilabel>, <guilabel>Emergency</guilabel>). The
<guibutton>Clear</guibutton> button empties the list.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</sect2>
</sect1>

</chapter>

<chapter id="configuration">
<title>Configuring &kappname;</title>

<para>
<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kappname;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
opens the configuration dialog.
</para>

<sect1 id="configure-mcp-servers">
<title>MCP Servers</title>
<para>
The <guilabel>MCP Servers</guilabel> page lists the configured servers. You can
add, modify, remove, enable or disable a server. Changes are saved immediately
and the server tabs of the main window are updated.
</para>
</sect1>

</chapter>

<chapter id="commands">
<title>Command Reference</title>

<sect1 id="kapp-mainwindow">
<title>The Menus</title>

<sect2 id="file-menu">
<title>The File Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice>
<shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>
</menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para><action>Quits</action> &kappname;.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="settings-menu">
<title>The Settings Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice>
<shortcut><keycombo action="simul"><keycap>F11</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Full Screen Mode</guimenuitem>
</menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para><action>Toggles</action> the full screen mode.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice>
<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Window Color Scheme</guisubmenu>
</menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para><action>Selects</action> the color scheme of the window.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice>
<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Notifications…</guimenuitem>
</menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para><action>Configures</action> the notifications of &kappname;.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice>
<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kappname;…</guimenuitem>
</menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para><action>Opens</action> the <link linkend="configuration">configuration dialog</link>.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>
&kappname; also has the common &kde; <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu items,
for more information read the section about the <ulink url="help:/fundamentals/menus.html#menus-settings">Settings Menu</ulink>
of the &kde; Fundamentals.
</para>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="help-menu">
<title>The Help Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice>
<guimenu>Help</guimenu><guimenuitem>What's new</guimenuitem>
</menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para><action>Shows</action> the new features of each release.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>
On &Windows; and &macOS;, the <guimenu>Help</guimenu> menu also contains an
item to check whether a new version is available.
</para>
<para>
&kappname; has the common &kde; <guimenu>Help</guimenu> menu items, for more
information read the section about the <ulink url="help:/fundamentals/menus.html#menus-help">Help Menu</ulink>
of the &kde; Fundamentals.
</para>
</sect2>

</sect1>
</chapter>

